{"kind":"request","text":"Add a typed fold over field types as the public seam for schema adapters, proved first by a Counter spike under foldkit.\n\nFiled 2026-11-11 19:49 EST from a design review with Hugh. Every fact below is read at main `df41e599`. This request follows the neutral `Form` request that it rests on. It adds public exports, so the stable-base order (`fc7576f8`) parks it until Hugh opens the adapter direction. It asks the planner to hold it with enough detail to schedule later.\n\n## Background\n\nHugh asked whether the view in \"Compiling to Categories\" (Elliott, 2017) gives a simpler integration with foldkit, a TypeScript framework on Effect that implements The Elm Architecture. Plan 035 already applied that view inside `packages/derive`: one admitted program with three interpretations.\n\nA dap definition and a foldkit program have the same shape:\n\n- State or a projection is the `Model`. `applyEntry` is `update`. `views` is `view`.\n- A head stream is a `Subscription`. A `tell` story is a `story` test.\n- An intent is a proposal, so an act maps to a Command, not to a Message. The `Answer` becomes the Command's result Messages. Foldkit fixes the Command error type to `never`, so a refusal is a typed Message, and dap's declared reasons supply the type.\n\nFoldkit requires an Effect Schema for the Model, for Command arguments and for Subscription dependencies. The one missing piece is therefore `FieldType` as a schema. Dap already writes that traversal by hand: six functions fold a `FieldType` into a different result, and two type-level mappings (`ValueOf` in `packages/client/src/declared.ts`, `NativeInputValue` in `packages/define/src/field-input.ts`) repeat each other.\n\n## The work\n\nRun part 1 first. Its result decides whether parts 2 to 4 land.\n\n1. **Spike, outside the repository.** Run the Counter definition under foldkit with a private Effect Schema algebra. The Model is the projection. Each act is one `Command.define` with `messages: [TookEffect, Refused, Unavailable]`. One Subscription wraps `observeScope`. No Effect dependency enters dap.\n2. **`foldField` in `packages/bytes`.** Export `foldField(algebra, type)` and `FieldAlgebra\u003cR\u003e`, with one case per `FieldType` member and an explicit `mark` case for a platform mark.\n3. **Two algebras.** Add a neutral JSON Schema algebra that describes native values. MCP's `schemaOf` becomes that algebra with two overridden cases, `member` and detached `text`, plus descriptions. Convert `typeWords`. Both lose `FieldLike` and their `default:` branches.\n4. **One `ValueOf` in `packages/contract`.** The client's `ValueOf` and define's `NativeInputValue` derive from it. An Effect algebra needs this type for its result, `Schema.Schema\u003cValueOf\u003cT\u003e\u003e`.\n\n## Not converted\n\n`fitsFieldType` and `mostBytes` are typed `switch` statements in kernel code and are already exhaustive. `fieldAssignable` compares two types. The two parsers of a declared type read unknown JSON. A fold does not apply to any of them.\n\n## What to weigh\n\n- **It is a feature.** `foldField`, `FieldAlgebra` and `ValueOf` are new public SDK exports. The wind-down parks features.\n- **It removes no code.** The gain is the compiler: a new `FieldType` case fails in every algebra, inside the repository and outside it. An adapter for Effect Schema, Zod or JSON Schema becomes one algebra. About 30 lines each is an estimate from reading `schemaOf`.\n- **The spike costs nothing in the repository.** It can run at any time and tests the direction before any export changes.\n- **Hosts.** A generic foldkit renderer for `ViewData` would host any package with no package code. That renderer is a later request and is not asked here.\n- **Kernel.** No kernel file changes and no record form is added.","body":{"conditions":"A Counter spike outside the repository runs join, say and one refusal under foldkit, and one foldkit story test resolves a Command with Refused and no scope; the planner records whether parts 2 to 4 proceed; if they proceed, foldField and FieldAlgebra are exported from packages/bytes with a mark case, typeWords and the JSON Schema algebra take no FieldLike and have no default branch, one ValueOf lives in packages/contract, docs/mcp-tools.json is unchanged, and npm run gate passes.","target_head":"df41e59964f09ce1d723ce870f5e4e5c6d8d4641","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}